# Endings: checked in this order on arrival day; the last one has no conditions.
# Each ending is one carrier clause (the fleet's hail vote) times one arrival clause
# (the storm vote: held the plan, waited it out in orbit, or no storm). Every ending
# closes on the first crate. `title` is the heading; see STORY_BIBLE.md.

card end_lights
type ending
cat ending
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when is B abort_who
title Lights On
when flag signal_answered
when flag arrive_hold
text Pre-dawn, the only slot the storm leaves. At midnight, over the link the handshake opened, the flight director clears one command, lights only, and {A} sends it. Two kilometres up, the dust turns white from below: Cargo 2, spending the battery it saved on every floodlight. Seven pilots, blind in their plumes, check radar against one glow. {B} sets down closest. By dawn the glow is one lamp. At noon {B} is at the window when it goes out. The first crate it carried says, in Sharpie: "You'll thank me." To Starbase: "Landed. All seven. The eighth kept the lights on." From a loading bay: "Told them it sulks."

card end_through
type ending
cat ending
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when is B abort_who
title Through the Dust
when flag arrive_hold
text Blind in dust, pilots fly radar for height and Cargo 2's knock for bearing, a fix every eleven seconds. The gust catches {B}'s ship: it stands on the slope on a folded strut and will not fly home. {B} sits on the bottom rung and starts a list of what it can still be: habitat, store, radio mast. Two sols later its battery rides a sled up the rim, and {A}, who wanted to answer all along, clips it to Cargo 2's port, answers inside the tick, then the HOLD off the laminated card. One lamp burns steady. {B} adds a line to the list: neighbour. To Starbase: "Landed. Seven down, six to fly." From a loading bay: "Tell it the bay says hello."

card end_long_orbit
type ending
cat ending
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when is B wait_who
title The Long Orbit
when flag signal_answered
when flag arrive_wait
text Week three in the long orbit, half rations on seven galley tables. Below, the storm, and one lamp, steady since the handshake; the storm starves the wing. Its manifest comes a line a pass. Tonight: tank liners, a glove, a drill bit. Seven hungry people cheer a drill bit. Next pass: seed stock, frozen in week two. The budget held a lamp or a hold heater, not both, and the fleet asked for the lamp. {B}, who argued to wait, logs it. When the storm clears, {B} flies first, the lamp in the window, calling the numbers for six. To Starbase: "Landed. All seven. The eighth was waiting." From a loading bay: "Thank it for the drill bit."

card end_patience
type ending
cat ending
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when is B ow_theory
title Patience
when flag arrive_wait
text Dawn on the rim, frost on the wing. All seven ships came down last night. For two weeks, past every chart, a battery under that frost has been choosing which knock to skip, and the strobe went dark at midnight. {A} kneels at the service port with a pack and a radio, {B} a step behind, counting. Eleven: nothing. Twenty-two: nothing. {A} clips the pack on anyway. Thirty-three: a click, slow, like something clearing its throat. The answer goes in by hand inside the tick, then the HOLD off the laminated card. Its lamp comes on and stays. To Starbase: "Landed. All seven. The eighth is warm." From a loading bay: "Knew it'd keep."

card end_friend
type ending
cat ending
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when is B ow_theory
title Sit With It
when flag signal_answered
text Second sol, halfway to Cargo 2 for its drill spares, {A} driving, {B} on the battery: forty-eight percent used, and the reserve rule says turn round; there and back ends far under the floor, unless Cargo 2 still charges trucks. The waiver takes eighteen minutes: YOUR CALL. {A} drives on. Cargo 2 hears them and lights its floods and the port at its foot. In marker: "Slow charger. Sit with it." {B} plugs in at four percent. They sit with it all afternoon, on the charge it kept for the cold, and load the spares gently. Its lamp is dimmer that night, for good. To Starbase: "Landed. All eight." From a loading bay: "Told you it was slow."

card end_close
type ending
cat ending
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when is B ow_theory
title Close Enough
text Third sol, two hundred metres from Cargo 2, {A} and {B} in the cab. On the first sol Cargo 3's drill snapped its only bit; the spare is in that hold. The rover's spare batteries went to heaters on the second night. {A} counts the dark, nine, ten, eleven, and answers. HELLO RX · OK. The cargo doors unlatch. Cargo 2 obeys its patch, WAKE ALL: every heater at once, no battery check. The HOLD goes out on the next tick. By then it has nothing left to hear it with. They drive back heaters off, the bit in {B}'s lap. To Starbase: "Landed. All seven. Found the eighth. In time for the bit." From a loading bay: "Told them. Thank it for us."

